# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend API base URL (Railway / Render deployment URL in production).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api-spinr.spinr.ca

# Server-side backend URL (used by API route handlers; falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL if unset). Should be the internal service URL in prod.
# REQUIRED in production — missing value throws at module load time ([18-4]).
BACKEND_URL=https://api-spinr.spinr.ca

# ── Public tracking domain ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated hostnames that serve ONLY the public ride-tracking page.
# On these hosts, track.spinr.ca/{token} is rewritten to /track/{token} and
# every admin route (login, dashboard) returns 404. The admin panel is served
# on its own domain (e.g. admin-spinr.spinr.ca). Defaults to track.spinr.ca.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKING_HOSTS=track.spinr.ca

# Google Maps JavaScript API key for the tracking page (tiles + Directions).
# PUBLIC, HTTP-referrer-restricted key — same value as the mobile apps'
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY. Restrict it to the tracking domain in the
# Google Cloud Console → Credentials page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Maps: MapLibre basemaps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The public /track/<token> page uses the Google Maps JS API (key above). These
# settings drive the *admin dashboard's* MapLibre maps — ride Route Views, Live
# Monitoring, heat map — which still use the provider chain below.
#
# Chain order (basemapChain() in src/lib/map/maplibre-base.ts), first hop wins
# and the rest stay behind it as fallbacks:
#   0. NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL  — your own tile server. When set it is the
#                                   ONLY hop; nothing sits behind it.
#   1. OpenFreeMap                — keyless default, used when 0 is unset.
#   2. Protomaps hosted           — only when the key below is set.
#
# Carto was hop 3 ("keyless, independent host, always last") until 2026-09-14,
# when the third-party basemaps were removed. It was the only keyless hop, so
# with no Protomaps key the unconfigured chain is now OpenFreeMap alone.
#
# Protomaps hosted key. This is a PUBLIC, domain-restricted key (like a Google
# Maps JS key) — it ships in the browser, so it belongs here, NOT in the backend
# app_settings table. Restrict it to your tracking domain in the Protomaps
# dashboard.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROTOMAPS_API_KEY=7ee89ce997b4ee94
# Basemap flavor: light | dark | white | grayscale | black
NEXT_PUBLIC_PROTOMAPS_FLAVOR=light

# ── Maps: self-hosting (deploy/tiles) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Stand up deploy/tiles and point these at it to stop depending on third-party
# basemaps. Both are optional and independent — set one, both, or neither;
# anything unset keeps the third-party default above.
#
# NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD time. Changing these in Vercel
# needs a redeploy, not just a restart.
#
# Vector style — when set it becomes the admin basemap chain's ONLY hop. The
# maps therefore go blank, rather than degrading to a third party, if your tile
# server is unreachable. Set this once the service is bedded in, not before.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL=https://tiles-spinr.spinr.ca/styles/basemap/style.json
#
# Optional dark counterpart. Unset, dark mode uses the light style above rather
# than dropping to a third party.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL_DARK=https://tiles-spinr.spinr.ca/styles/basemap-dark/style.json
#
# Rasterised PNG tiles for the no-WebGL fallback renderer (static-route-map.tsx,
# which draws plain <img> tiles when a browser extension stubs WebGL). Vector
# self-hosting alone cannot feed it. {z}/{x}/{y} are substituted.
#
# There is no third-party default any more. Left unset, it is DERIVED from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL — but only when that ends in /style.json, i.e. is a
# tileserver-gl style document with a sibling PNG pyramid. Point the vector
# variable at any other provider and there is no raster source at all; the
# renderer then says "No basemap configured" instead of 404ing every tile. Set
# this one explicitly for anything that is not tileserver-gl.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RASTER_TILE_URL=https://tiles-spinr.spinr.ca/styles/basemap/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#
# Verify a tile server serves all of the above before wiring it up:
#   TILES_URL=https://tiles-spinr.spinr.ca deploy/tiles/smoke-test.sh

# ── Sentry (optional but recommended) ───────────────────────────────────────
# [22-2] PIPEDA data residency: Sentry has no Canadian region. EU
# (https://o<org>.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project>) is the closest compliant option
# and remains the target. Spinr's org is in the US region (accepted risk, DPA
# addendum required) — see docs/change-log/2026-08-05-sentry-us-region-accepted.md.
# Set in Vercel project settings → Environment Variables.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_DSN=

# Injected automatically by Vercel at build time — do not set manually.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=

# ── Firebase App Check (public driver-registration page) ────────────────────
# The web driver self-registration flow (/register/driver, unauthenticated by
# design) needs its own App Check attestation, separate from the mobile apps'
# Play Integrity/DeviceCheck — web uses reCAPTCHA Enterprise instead. All
# four values below are PUBLIC, client-embedded values (same category as the
# Maps/Protomaps keys above), safe to ship in the browser bundle. Get them
# from Firebase Console:
#   1. Project Settings → Your apps → add a Web app (if none exists yet) for
#      the same Firebase project the mobile apps use → copy its config values
#      into the four NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* vars below.
#   2. Build → App Check → register that Web app → reCAPTCHA Enterprise (the
#      classic "reCAPTCHA" v3 option is greyed out in Firebase Console as of
#      2026-09 — Firebase has stopped accepting new classic registrations) →
#      copy the site key into NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY below. No
#      separate secret key is needed: Enterprise verifies tokens via the
#      reCAPTCHA Enterprise API using this project's own GCP credentials.
# Left unset, appCheckHeader() (src/lib/firebase-app-check.ts) fails open —
# no header is sent, and this page's uploads behave exactly as they did
# before this fix. It only helps once all five values are set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# ── Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# JWT secret must match the backend JWT_SECRET. Only needed if the
# admin-dashboard ever validates tokens server-side (currently it does not).
# JWT_SECRET=

# ── Vercel / CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set in Vercel project settings or GitHub Actions secrets.
# VERCEL_TOKEN=
# VERCEL_ORG_ID=
# VERCEL_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=
